.Dd September 21, 2026
.Dt RECOVERY 7
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm recovery
.Nd recovery system and repair procedures
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The recovery system runs from a RAM root.
It boots from the install stick's first partition or the disk's recovery
entry.
To select the latter from the running system, use
.Ql bootctl trial recovery
and reboot.
.Pp
The recovery kernel permits root to write
.Pa /dev/diskN
and uses the read-write driver policy.
The recovery system mounts nothing from the disk it repairs.
.Ss Startup
The recovery system runs
.Pa /sbin/init
built as
.Ql init-recovery .
It starts a shell on the console without a login: the image has no
accounts of the machine's to check against.
It starts the SSH server only when a key was built into the image, and
reports which on the console:
.Dl init: a key was built into this recovery image, so SSH is on
.Dl init: no key was built into this recovery image, so SSH is off
With
.Ql rach2.fsck
on the boot line, init first runs
.Ql e2fsck -p
on each of
.Pa /dev/disk0p1
through
.Pa /dev/disk0p4
whose superblock has the ext2 magic, and reports
.Dl init: e2fsck: /dev/disk0pN: status S
Status 0 means clean, 1 repaired, 4 faults left and 8 an error.
Without the token a recovery boot repairs nothing.
The network is configured by the kernel from the
.Ql rach2.ip=
boot setting, or by DHCP when that setting is
.Ql none .
.Ss Programs
The recovery image includes
.Nm rach2-install ,
.Nm rach2-recover ,
.Nm reflash ,
.Nm bootctl ,
.Nm growroot ,
.Nm growset ,
.Nm growboot ,
.Nm diskctl ,
.Nm e2fsck ,
.Nm resize2fs ,
.Nm update ,
.Nm rescue-static ,
.Nm ping ,
.Nm dmesg
and the BusyBox tools.
.Ss Update procedures
The procedure depends on what is being replaced:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Kernel
From the running system, run
.Ql bootctl kernel FILE ,
reboot, read
.Ql bootctl status
and run
.Ql bootctl commit .
.It Root file system
From recovery, run
.Ql rach2-install --update IMAGE /dev/diskN .
Mount the install stick's exFAT partition and use its
.Pa rach2-metal-disk.ext2
as
.Ar IMAGE ;
the RAM root cannot store this 1 GiB file.
This preserves the accounts, SSH policy and keys.
The recovery archive stores account files and SSH policy under
.Pa rach2-config/etc ,
host keys under
.Pa rach2-config/etc/dropbear ,
and each account's home
.Pa .ssh
contents under
.Pa rach2-config/keys/UID .
Root's keys use UID 0.
The home comes from passwd, and only the first entry for a shared UID
supplies keys.
Numeric directory names cannot collide by case on FAT32.
A resumed update, or one whose old root cannot be read, restores these keys
from the archive, with modes 700 for directories and 600 for files.
Host keys are owned by 0:0; account keys return to the home from the
archived passwd with its uid and gid.
Missing homes are created with mode 700 and that owner.
Keys for UIDs absent from that file are ignored.
An older archive without UID key directories cannot restore account keys.
The installer builds and syncs
.Pa rach2-config.new ,
renames the current archive to
.Pa rach2-config.old ,
then promotes the new copy and syncs before removing the old one.
Before any archive read or write, a missing current archive is recovered
from a new copy containing all three account files, or otherwise from the
old copy when present.
The new copy is never removed unless a current archive exists.
Recovery remains the saved default until the trial root has been verified;
then run
.Ql bootctl commit .
.It Recovery partition
Use
.Xr reflash 8
from the disk's recovery entry.
The partition being written is not mounted.
The saved default remains the candidate for this write.
A torn write is repaired from the install stick.
.El
.Pp
The machine's disk stays in its bay.
These procedures run over SSH or at the console.
Do not make a write that cannot be undone from the stick.
The install stick has room beside its two images for saved copies of
the 64 MiB boot and recovery partitions.
This reserve does not cover a backup of a grown root.
Check the space required by the actual save set before writing.
.Ss Recovery menu
.Xr rach2-recover 8
offers these choices:
.Bl -enum
.It
List the machine's disks, with model, serial, size in bytes, partition table
and partitions.
.It
Check a file system.
.It
Put a saved image back on a disk.
.It
Install a kernel on a boot partition.
.It
Start a shell.
.It
Leave.
.El
.Pp
Each step can be left without taking action and reports its result in one
line.
.Ss Kernel debug shell
The boot option
.Ql rach2.rescue
skips init and enters the kernel debug shell.
Its
.Ql exec PROGRAM
command runs a program from the root.
The console belongs to the shell.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /root/.ssh/authorized_keys
.It Pa /etc/rach2/sshd.conf
SSH policy, including the
.Ql root-password-login
setting.
.It Pa /root/.ssh/authorized_keys
Root's SSH authorized keys.
.It Pa /proc/disk
Disk records.
.It Pa /proc/cmdline
The boot command line.
.It Pa /dev/bootlog
The boot log.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr disk 7 ,
.Xr bootctl 8 ,
.Xr growroot 8 ,
.Xr rach2-install 8 ,
.Xr rach2-recover 8 ,
.Xr reflash 8
